<%# "Who has been busiest here" — the question a Who sort would have answered
    badly even if it were possible (it is not; actor names are encrypted). A sort
    clusters names alphabetically and then asks the reader to spot which block is
    tallest, across pages. A count states it.

    Counts come from a grouped count over the whole filtered scope, so they are
    the number of rows that MATCHED, not the number on this page. Read them as
    "Ada did 30 of the things this filter describes", not "30 are visible". %>
<div data-role="top-actors" class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
  <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-text-heading"><%= t("operations.activity_logs.index.top_actors.label") %></h2>
  <ul role="list" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <% @top_actors.each do |actor, count| %>
      <li data-role="top-actor">
        <%# A way INTO the ledger, not a decoration on top of it — and through the
            same `q` pivot the row details use, so there is one way to narrow to a
            person rather than two that behave differently.

            _top: the pivot sets the search box, which lives in the band OUTSIDE
            the results frame; a frame-local swap would leave the box blank while
            the rows changed underneath it.

            aria-label: out of context "Ada Lovelace 30" says nothing about what
            following it does. The visible words stay inside the name (2.5.3). %>
        <%= link_to operations_activity_logs_path(ledger_filter_params(q: actor.email_address)),
              data: { turbo_frame: "_top", focus_key: "q" },
              class: "inline-flex min-h-input items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-border px-3 py-1 " \
                     "text-sm text-text-body hover:bg-surface-sunken focus-ring",
              "aria-label": t("operations.activity_logs.index.top_actors.entry_aria_label",
                              name: actor.full_name, count: count) do %>
          <span><%= actor.full_name %></span>
          <span class="tabular-nums font-semibold text-text-heading"><%= count %></span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</div>
